,title,link,text,language,family
0,Pentlatch language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pentlatch_language,"May 29, 2025 - The Pentlatch, Pentl’ach, Puntlatch, Puntlatsh or Puntledge language is a Salishan language that is spoken on Canada's Vancouver Island in a small area between Comox and Nanaimo, British Columbia. The Pentlatch people formerly numbered at least 3,000 with at least 90 settlements in the area.",Pentlatch,Salish
1,Coast Salish peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast_Salish,"5 days ago - The Coast Salish peoples are a group of ethnically and linguistically related Indigenous peoples of the Pacific Northwest Coast, living in the Canadian province of British Columbia and the U.S. states of Washington and Oregon. They speak the Coast Salish languages and Tsamosan languages.",Pentlatch,Salish
2,Coast Salish languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast_Salish_languages,"February 4, 2026 - The Coast Salish languages, also known as the Central Salish languages, are a branch of the Salishan language family. These languages are spoken by First Nations or Native American peoples inhabiting the Pacific Northwest, in the territory that is now known as the southwest coast of British ...",Pentlatch,Salish
3,Pentlatch language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/pentlatch_language,"Overall, early recordings prioritized breadth over depth, capturing Pentlatch's isolate-like traits within Central Salish while highlighting the challenges of documenting moribund varieties under colonial disruption.",Pentlatch,Salish
4,Reawakening Pentlatch - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cIVG9LOQCpM,"Apr 22, 2025 · Carrie and Megan talk with the Working Pentlatch Revitalization team (Mathew Andreatta ( / xixa_niyus ) , Jessie Recalma ( / saatlamarts ) , Chief Michael Recalma...",Pentlatch,Salish
5,Pentlatch People Flood: Queneesh - Episode 6 of 9 ... - YouTubePentlatch Puntledge Qualicum First Nation Portal WebsitesIt was deemed extinct. But now pentl'ach has been declared a ...Coast Salish - playlist by Rosie | Spotify,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Kf5EPdU3p8w,"Jun 27, 2026 · Most Coast Salish Nations have a flood account that anchors their people to a prominent local mountain. For the Pentlatch people, the legend of Queneesh tells the story of a spiritual being... Find portal websites to the Pentlatch Puntledge Qualicum Indians of British Columbia, Canada with First Nations Seeker's Pentlatch page! Dec 2, 2023 · Long considered extinct, pentl'ach has now been declared a living language and added to British Columbia's official list of First Nations languages. Sign up to get unlimited songs and podcasts with occasional ads. No credit card needed.",Pentlatch,Salish
