7,Pentlatch - Coast Salish and Neighboring Languages - Library Guides at University of Washington Libraries,https://guides.lib.uw.edu/c.php?g=1002741&p=7277310,"April 14, 2026 - Coast Salish and Neighboring Languages · Pentlatch · M. Dale Kinkade papers · > Last Updated: Jun 13, 2024 3:45 PM · URL: https://guides.lib.uw.edu/coastsalishlanguages · Print Page ·",Pentlatch,Salish
8,Northern Coast Salish | The Canadian Encyclopedia,https://www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/salish-northern-georgia-strait-coast,"The potlatch was (and still is) a cultural ceremony significant to not only the Northern Coast Salish peoples but other Indigenous peoples of the Northwest Coast. During the potlatch, property and gifts are distributed to guests.",Pentlatch,Salish
9,"Pentlatch Language and the Pentlatch Indian Tribe (Puntlatch, Pentlach, Qualicum)",http://www.native-languages.org/pentlatch.htm,"Pentlatch was a Salishan language of British Columbia, closely related to Comox. Though there are still people of Pentlatch descent today, the Pentlatch language was last spoken in the 1940's, and few records of it remain.",Pentlatch,Salish
